Let simdutf build against MSVC's STL from a clang it doesn't expect yet.

MSVC 14.52 (GitHub's windows-2025-vs2026 image from 20261111) static_asserts
"STL1000: Unexpected compiler version, expected Clang 22 or newer", and Zig
0.16 ships clang 21. On MSVC, simdutf is the C++ that includes STL headers
(Ghostty skips linkLibCpp there), so it alone fails. The STL's documented
escape hatch, `_ALLOW_COMPILER_AND_STL_VERSION_MISMATCH`, turns the check off.

illogical applies this at build time (vendor/libghostty-vt-sys/build.rs,
Arugula #1187) until Zig ships clang 22.

--- a/pkg/simdutf/build.zig
+++ b/pkg/simdutf/build.zig
@@ -69,6 +69,9 @@
         // On MSVC we skip linkLibCpp (see above), so the C++ standard is
         // not set implicitly. simdutf requires C++17, so set it explicitly.
         try flags.append(b.allocator, "-std=c++17");
+        // MSVC 14.52's STL rejects clang older than 22 (STL1000), and
+        // Zig 0.16 ships clang 21.
+        try flags.append(b.allocator, "-D_ALLOW_COMPILER_AND_STL_VERSION_MISMATCH");
     }
 
     if (target.result.os.tag == .freebsd or
